IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`

-- g3-art8-register.l4: Article 8 (Charity register): the register and its three sections, the items entered for a registered charity (8(3)),
-- the principal address (8(4)), the items entered in the historic section (8(5)) and the ten-year retention of copies (8(6)).
-- Conventions of this module.
--   * Time unit of the DEONTIC rules: a trace on dates is stamped with DATE_SERIAL, so a day is one unit.
--   * A discretion of the Commissioner or the Minister ("approved by the Commissioner", "prescribed by the Minister by Order") is an input; the content of an Order is an input.
--   * Every public decision that depends on a reading takes `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` as an ordinary GIVEN and delegates by CONSIDER to one private function per reading.
--   * Facts that another group decides are GIVENs under the standard names of PLAN section (c): `the entity`, `the registered charity`, `the day`,
--     `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)`, `the required steps notices served`,
--     `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`, `the basis of deregistration`.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `Article 8(1): the Commissioner establishes and maintains the register`

-- src:217 | (1) The Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities.
@ref Article 8(1) (src:217)
@export The Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities (Article 8(1)); stands until the Commissioner does so
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(1) the Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `establish and maintain a register of charities`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(1): the Commissioner did not establish and maintain a register of charities"

§§ `Article 8(2): the general, restricted and historic sections`

-- The passive "must be kept" names no actor; the Commissioner, who establishes and maintains the register under paragraph (1), is the one who keeps it.
-- src:218 | (2) The register must be kept in such a way as to distinguish between –
-- src:219 | (a) the general section;
-- src:220 | (b) the restricted section; and
-- src:221 | (c) the historic section.
@ref Article 8(2) (src:218-221)
@export The register must be kept so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections (Article 8(2)); the actor is the Commissioner by Article 8(1)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(2) the register must be kept so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `keep the register so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(2): the register was not kept so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections"

-- The section of the register that a stored standing (domain.l4) names; an entity that is not on the register, or is only an applicant, is in no section.
@ref Article 1 "registered charity", Article 8(2)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Section of the register`
`the section named by the standing` standing MEANS
    CONSIDER standing
    WHEN `not on the register` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN JUST `the general section`
    WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN JUST `the restricted section`
    WHEN `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` THEN JUST `the historic section`

-- "Registered charity" (Article 1) is an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section; the historic section is excluded (trap T7).
-- This is the standing-level form of IP6; G1's `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` is the producer the integrator wires, and checks against this.
@ref Article 1 "registered charity", Article 8(2)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the standing is that of a registered charity` standing MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section named by the standing` standing
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST section THEN section EQUALS `the general section` OR section EQUALS `the restricted section`

-- F3.6: a placement takes effect on the day of the entry, or on the day after.  One private function per reading; the public one delegates by CONSIDER.
@ref Article 8(2), 8(3)(g), 8(5)(d) (fork F3.6)
GIVEN placement IS A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.6 reading A: an entry takes effect on the day of the entry` placement `the day` MEANS
    placement's `date of the entry` AT MOST `the day`

@ref Article 8(2), 8(3)(g), 8(5)(d) (fork F3.6)
GIVEN placement IS A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.6 reading B: an entry takes effect on the day after the entry` placement `the day` MEANS
    placement's `date of the entry` LESS THAN `the day`

@ref Article 8(2), 8(3)(g), 8(5)(d) (fork F3.6)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      placement IS A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the placement has taken effect by` interp placement `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `day on which an entry takes effect`
    WHEN `on the day of the entry` THEN `F3.6 reading A: an entry takes effect on the day of the entry` placement `the day`
    WHEN `on the day after the entry` THEN `F3.6 reading B: an entry takes effect on the day after the entry` placement `the day`

-- The latest of a list of placements; of two on the same day, the one listed later.
@ref Article 8(2)
GIVEN placements IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
`the latest placement among` placements MEANS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, p YIELD
              CONSIDER acc
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST p
              WHEN JUST q THEN IF q's `date of the entry` GREATER THAN p's `date of the entry` THEN JUST q ELSE JUST p)
          NOTHING
          placements

@ref Article 8(2) (src:218-221)
@export The section of the register (general, restricted or historic) in which an entity is entered on a day, from its dated entries; NOTHING if it is in no section on that day
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      placements IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` @desc Every entry of the entity in a section of the register, with its date; empty if it has never been entered
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
GIVETH A MAYBE `Section of the register`
`Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` interp placements `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the latest placement among` (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `the placement has taken effect by` interp p `the day`) placements)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST latest THEN JUST (latest's `the section`)

§§ `Article 8(3)(a): the note of the status of the entity`

-- Sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of Article 2(1), by constructor and never by position (domain.l4 lists (ba) third).  F3.13: whether (ba) is treated like them.
@ref Article 8(3)(a) (fork F3.13)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sub-paragraph (ba) is treated like the sub-paragraphs the note names` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)`
    WHEN `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Article 8(3)(a) treats sub-paragraph (ba) like sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) for the note of sub-paragraph (a) and like (e), (g), (h) and (j) for the details` THEN TRUE

-- src:224 | (i) the sub-paragraph of the definition “entity” in Article 2(1) within which the entity falls (including, in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of that definition, whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)), and
@ref Article 8(3)(a)(i), "(f) to (j)" (src:224)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      kind IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of Article 2(1)` interp kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE                                                                                                         -- (f)
    WHEN `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN TRUE                    -- (g)
    WHEN `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` THEN TRUE                -- (h)
    WHEN `an unincorporated body or association of persons` THEN TRUE                                                                  -- (i)
    WHEN `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction` THEN TRUE            -- (j)
    WHEN `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` THEN `sub-paragraph (ba) is treated like the sub-paragraphs the note names` interp
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:225 | (ii) in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) or (j) of that definition, details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law, by virtue of which it falls within that sub-paragraph;
@ref Article 8(3)(a)(ii), "(e), (g), (h) or (j)" (src:225)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      kind IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) and (j) of Article 2(1)` interp kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` THEN TRUE                              -- (e)
    WHEN `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN TRUE                    -- (g)
    WHEN `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` THEN TRUE                -- (h)
    WHEN `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction` THEN TRUE            -- (j)
    WHEN `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` THEN `sub-paragraph (ba) is treated like the sub-paragraphs the note names` interp
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Trap T5: sub-paragraph (ba) was inserted by R&O.56/2025 and Article 8(3)(a) was not amended, so on the reading taken a (ba) entity gets no "also within (a)" note
-- and no (ii) details: "none required by Article 8(3)(a)(ii)".  The gap is reported as fork F3.13 and as a contradiction in FRAGMENT-G3.md.
-- src:223 | (a) a note of the status of the entity that is the registered charity, being –
-- src:224 | (i) the sub-paragraph of the definition “entity” in Article 2(1) within which the entity falls (including, in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of that definition, whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)), and
-- src:225 | (ii) in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) or (j) of that definition, details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law, by virtue of which it falls within that sub-paragraph;
@ref Article 8(3)(a) (src:223-225)
@export What the note of the status of an entity must say (Article 8(3)(a)): the sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) it falls within, whether an entity within (f) to (j) also falls within (a), and the sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h), (j) for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity, with its kinds of entity under Article 2(1) as G1 derives them
GIVETH A `Requirement of the note of status (Article 8(3)(a))`
`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` interp `the entity` MEANS
    `Requirement of the note of status (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls` IS `the entity`'s `kinds of entity`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` IS
            IF any (GIVEN k YIELD `the kind is one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of Article 2(1)` interp k) (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)
            THEN JUST (elem `the trustees of a trust` (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`))
            ELSE NOTHING
        `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required` IS
            filter (GIVEN k YIELD `the kind is one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) and (j) of Article 2(1)` interp k) (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)

-- Whether a recorded note is the note the Article requires: the same sub-paragraphs, the same answer to "also within (a)", and details wherever details are required.
@ref Article 8(3)(a)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the note of status (Article 8(3)(a))`
      recorded IS A `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` requirement recorded MEANS
        all (GIVEN k YIELD elem k (recorded's `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded`)) (requirement's `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls`)
    AND all (GIVEN k YIELD elem k (requirement's `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls`)) (recorded's `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded`)
    AND recorded's `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` EQUALS requirement's `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)`
    AND (null (requirement's `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
         OR isJust (recorded's `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law`))

§§ `Article 8(3)(b) to (n): which items are entered for a registered charity`

-- src:226 | (b) the names of each of the governors of the registered charity;
@ref Article 8(3)(b) (src:226)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` `the entity` MEANS
    map (GIVEN g YIELD g's name) (`the entity`'s governors)

-- "Other" premises are premises other than the one at the principal address entered under paragraph (3)(c): two premises with one address are one premises.
@ref Article 8(3)(d)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
      premises IS A `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the premises are at the principal address entered` facts premises MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `principal address entered`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST address THEN address EQUALS premises's address

-- src:228 | (d) the address of any other premises in Jersey, other than a private dwelling house, at or from which the registered charity undertakes any activity;
@ref Article 8(3)(d) (src:228)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` facts MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD p's address)
        (filter (GIVEN p YIELD     p's `in Jersey`
                               AND NOT p's `a private dwelling house`
                               AND p's `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity`
                               AND NOT `the premises are at the principal address entered` facts p)
                (facts's `other premises`))

-- src:232 | (h) if the registered charity is an organized religious charity, within the meaning of Article 28, a note of that fact and of the provision of the Order under that Article by virtue of which it is such a charity;
@ref Article 8(3)(h) (src:232)
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3)(h) a note that the charity is an organized religious charity is required` `the registered charity` MEANS
    `the registered charity`'s `is an organized religious charity`

-- src:233 | (i) if the registered charity meets the charity test by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3), the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within paragraph (2) of that Article;
@ref Article 8(3)(i) (src:233)
GIVEN `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3)(i) the text of the provision in the constitution is required` `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` MEANS
    `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)`

-- F3.8: "if a required steps notice has been served".
@ref Article 8(3)(k) (fork F3.8)
GIVEN `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
`F3.8 reading A: every notice that has been served` `the required steps notices served` MEANS
    `the required steps notices served`

@ref Article 8(3)(k) (fork F3.8)
GIVEN `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
`F3.8 reading B: only a notice that has not been complied with` `the required steps notices served` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN n YIELD NOT n's `has been complied with`) `the required steps notices served`

-- src:235 | (k) if a required steps notice has been served on the registered charity, or on a governor of the registered charity, a note of that fact (or a copy of the notice) and of the date on which the notice was served;
@ref Article 8(3)(k) (src:235)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
`Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` interp `the required steps notices served` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `required steps notices noted`
    WHEN `every notice that has been served` THEN `F3.8 reading A: every notice that has been served` `the required steps notices served`
    WHEN `only a notice that has not been complied with` THEN `F3.8 reading B: only a notice that has not been complied with` `the required steps notices served`

-- src:236 | (l) if the registered name has been changed, the previous registered name or names;
@ref Article 8(3)(l) (src:236)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` facts MEANS
    facts's `previous registered names`

-- src:237 | (m) if an Order under Article 13(9)(c) applies to the registered charity, any details or statement that must be entered on the register under that Order; and
@ref Article 8(3)(m) (src:237)
GIVEN `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3)(m) the details or statement under the Order are required` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` MEANS
    `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`

-- The content of an Order is an input: a non-empty list means that an Order prescribes other information for the register.
-- src:238 | (n) any other information prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(3)(n) (src:238)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3)(n) other information prescribed by the Minister by Order is required` facts MEANS
    NOT null (facts's `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)`)

-- The fourteen items, in the Article's order.
@ref Article 8(3)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`the fourteen items of Article 8(3)` MEANS
    LIST `a note of the status of the entity`                                                                    -- (a)
       , `the names of each of the governors`                                                                    -- (b)
       , `the principal address`                                                                                 -- (c)
       , `the address of any other premises in Jersey`                                                           -- (d)
       , `the registered charitable purposes`                                                                    -- (e)
       , `the registered public benefit statement`                                                               -- (f)
       , `the date on which the charity was registered`                                                          -- (g)
       , `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity`                                             -- (h)
       , `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)`                          -- (i)
       , `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`                    -- (j)
       , `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`                              -- (k)
       , `the previous registered names`                                                                         -- (l)
       , `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`                   -- (m)
       , `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order`                                                 -- (n)

-- src:222 | (3) The Commissioner must enter in the register, in respect of each registered charity (whether entered in the general or restricted section), in addition to the registered name and registration number entered under Article 12(2) –
@ref Article 8(3) (src:222)
@export The items the Commissioner must enter in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3), (a) to (n)); empty if the charity is not entered in the general or restricted section
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, with the entity and its standing on the register
      `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the charity test only because an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc Every required steps notice served on the charity or on a governor of it; empty if none
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` @desc Other premises, the principal address entered, previous names and other information prescribed by Order
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` interp `the registered charity` `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts MEANS
    IF `the standing is that of a registered charity` (`the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register`)
    THEN filter required `the fourteen items of Article 8(3)`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        required item MEANS
            CONSIDER item
            WHEN `a note of the status of the entity` THEN TRUE                                                                            -- (a)
            WHEN `the names of each of the governors` THEN TRUE                                                                            -- (b)
            WHEN `the principal address` THEN TRUE                                                                                         -- (c)
            WHEN `the address of any other premises in Jersey` THEN NOT null (`Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` facts)   -- (d)
            WHEN `the registered charitable purposes` THEN TRUE                                                                            -- (e)
            WHEN `the registered public benefit statement` THEN TRUE                                                                       -- (f)
            WHEN `the date on which the charity was registered` THEN TRUE                                                                  -- (g)
            WHEN `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity` THEN `Art 8(3)(h) a note that the charity is an organized religious charity is required` `the registered charity`   -- (h)
            WHEN `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)` THEN `Art 8(3)(i) the text of the provision in the constitution is required` `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)`   -- (i)
            WHEN `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year` THEN TRUE                            -- (j)
            WHEN `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` THEN NOT null (`Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` interp `the required steps notices served`)   -- (k)
            WHEN `the previous registered names` THEN NOT null (`Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` facts)           -- (l)
            WHEN `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` THEN `Art 8(3)(m) the details or statement under the Order are required` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`   -- (m)
            WHEN `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order` THEN `Art 8(3)(n) other information prescribed by the Minister by Order is required` facts   -- (n)

-- The duty of Article 8(3): the Commissioner must enter every required item.  A conjunction of one duty per item (RAND); the empty list is FULFILLED.
-- The Article states no time: no WITHIN is written (BRIEF; patterns 5.9).  The item entered is the act, so the rule is typed by the act and not by the paragraph.
@ref Article 8(3)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`the Commissioner must enter each of` items MEANS
    CONSIDER items
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN item FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` item
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(3): a required item was not entered in the register for the registered charity")
        RAND `the Commissioner must enter each of` rest

-- src:222 | (3) The Commissioner must enter in the register, in respect of each registered charity (whether entered in the general or restricted section), in addition to the registered name and registration number entered under Article 12(2) –
@ref Article 8(3) (src:222)
@export The Commissioner must enter each item required by Article 8(3) in the register for a registered charity; a conjunction of one duty per item, and FULFILLED if no item is required
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, with the entity and its standing on the register
      `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the charity test only because an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc Every required steps notice served on the charity or on a governor of it; empty if none
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` @desc Other premises, the principal address entered, previous names and other information prescribed by Order
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(3) the Commissioner must enter in the register the entries required for the registered charity` interp `the registered charity` `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts MEANS
    `the Commissioner must enter each of`
        (`Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` interp `the registered charity` `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts)

-- What the register holds, item by item: is each required item entered?  The names, the other premises, the notices, the previous names and the prescribed
-- information are entered only if every one of them is.
@ref Article 8(3)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      entry IS AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))`
      `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
      item IS AN `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register entry holds the item` interp entry `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `a note of the status of the entity` THEN
        CONSIDER entry's `note of status`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST recorded THEN `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires`
                                    (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` interp (entry's `the registered charity`'s entity))
                                    recorded
    WHEN `the names of each of the governors` THEN
        all (GIVEN n YIELD elem n (entry's `names of the governors`)) (`Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` (entry's `the registered charity`'s entity))
    WHEN `the principal address` THEN isJust (entry's `principal address`)
    WHEN `the address of any other premises in Jersey` THEN
        all (GIVEN a YIELD elem a (entry's `addresses of other premises in Jersey`)) (`Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` facts)
    WHEN `the registered charitable purposes` THEN
        (NOT null (entry's `the registered charity`'s `registered charitable purposes`)) AND entry's `statement of purposes approved by the Commissioner`
    WHEN `the registered public benefit statement` THEN
        (NOT (entry's `the registered charity`'s `registered public benefit statement` EQUALS "")) AND entry's `public benefit statement approved by the Commissioner`
    WHEN `the date on which the charity was registered` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity` THEN isJust (entry's `note of the organized religious charity and of the provision of the Order`)
    WHEN `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)` THEN isJust (entry's `text of the provision of the constitution within Article 5(2)`)
    WHEN `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year` THEN isJust (entry's `annual return sent for the most recent year`)
    WHEN `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` THEN
        all (GIVEN n YIELD any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `served on` EQUALS n's `served on` AND r's `date served` EQUALS n's `date served`) (entry's `notes of required steps notices`))
            (`Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` interp `the required steps notices served`)
    WHEN `the previous registered names` THEN
        all (GIVEN n YIELD elem n (entry's `previous registered names`)) (`Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` facts)
    WHEN `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` THEN isJust (entry's `details or statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`)
    WHEN `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order` THEN
        all (GIVEN i YIELD elem i (entry's `other information prescribed by Order`)) (facts's `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)`)

@ref Article 8(3) (src:222)
@export Which items required by Article 8(3) are missing from the register entry of a registered charity; empty if the entry is complete
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      entry IS AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))` @desc What the register holds for the charity, item by item
      `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the charity test only because an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc Every required steps notice served on the charity or on a governor of it; empty if none
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` @desc Other premises, the principal address entered, previous names and other information prescribed by Order
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`Art 8(3) the items missing from the register entry` interp entry `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT `the register entry holds the item` interp entry `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts item)
           (`Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` interp (entry's `the registered charity`) `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3)` `the required steps notices served` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` facts)

§§ `Article 8(4): the principal address`

-- F3.9: which entities are "a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law to have a registered office or business address in Jersey".
-- Where Article 2(5) names no constitutional Law for the kind (trap T6), the caller gives FALSE for the requirement, so the cascade moves to (b).
@ref Article 8(4)(a) (fork F3.9)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.9 reading A: only an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have an office or address` `the entity` facts MEANS
    facts's `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey`

@ref Article 8(4)(a) (fork F3.9)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.9 reading B: every company and foundation, and any other entity that its constitutional Law so requires` `the entity` facts MEANS
        elem `a company` (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)
    OR elem `a foundation` (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)
    OR facts's `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey`

-- src:240 | (a) if the registered charity is a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law to have a registered office or business address in Jersey, the address of that registered office or that business address;
@ref Article 8(4)(a) (src:240)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` interp `the entity` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `entities within Article 8(4)(a)`
    WHEN `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey` THEN
        `F3.9 reading A: only an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have an office or address` `the entity` facts
    WHEN `every company and foundation, and any other entity that its constitutional Law so requires` THEN
        `F3.9 reading B: every company and foundation, and any other entity that its constitutional Law so requires` `the entity` facts

-- (b) and (c) for an entity that is not within (a).  F3.10: main premises that are a private dwelling house.
@ref Article 8(4)(b), (c) (fork F3.10)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`F3.10 reading A: Article 8(4)(b) does not apply to a private dwelling house, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached` facts MEANS
    facts's `addresses in Jersey of the governors`

@ref Article 8(4)(b), (c) (fork F3.10)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`F3.10 reading B: Article 8(4)(b) applies to a private dwelling house and gives no address` facts MEANS
    EMPTY

-- src:241 | (b) if the charity is not such an entity, the address of the main premises in Jersey at or from which the activities in Jersey of the registered charity are managed, controlled or undertaken, unless the premises are a private dwelling house; or
-- src:242 | (c) if neither sub-paragraph (a) nor (b) applies, the address in Jersey of one of the governors of the charity.
@ref Article 8(4)(b), (c) (src:241-242)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the addresses under Article 8(4)(b) and (c)` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN facts's `addresses in Jersey of the governors`
    WHEN JUST premises THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT premises's `in Jersey` THEN facts's `addresses in Jersey of the governors`
            IF NOT premises's `a private dwelling house` THEN LIST premises's address
            OTHERWISE
                CONSIDER interp's `main premises that are a private dwelling house`
                WHEN `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached` THEN `F3.10 reading A: Article 8(4)(b) does not apply to a private dwelling house, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached` facts
                WHEN `Article 8(4)(b) applies and gives no address` THEN `F3.10 reading B: Article 8(4)(b) applies to a private dwelling house and gives no address` facts

-- src:239 | (4) The principal address for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c) is –
-- src:240 | (a) if the registered charity is a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law to have a registered office or business address in Jersey, the address of that registered office or that business address;
-- src:241 | (b) if the charity is not such an entity, the address of the main premises in Jersey at or from which the activities in Jersey of the registered charity are managed, controlled or undertaken, unless the premises are a private dwelling house; or
-- src:242 | (c) if neither sub-paragraph (a) nor (b) applies, the address in Jersey of one of the governors of the charity.
@ref Article 8(4) (src:239-242)
@export The addresses in Jersey that may be entered as the principal address of a registered charity (Article 8(4)): the registered office or business address, else the main premises unless a private dwelling house, else the address in Jersey of one of the governors (so, any of those addresses)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity, with its kinds of entity under Article 2(1)
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc Whether its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey, that address, the main premises in Jersey, the governors' addresses in Jersey
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` interp `the entity` facts MEANS
    IF `Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` interp `the entity` facts
    THEN CONSIDER facts's `registered office or business address in Jersey`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
         WHEN JUST address THEN LIST address
    ELSE `the addresses under Article 8(4)(b) and (c)` interp facts

-- IP17: whether the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4) (consumed by G4, Article 11(4)(d)).
@ref Article 8(4) (src:239-242)
@export Whether the entity has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4) (the fact Article 11(4)(d) asks of an applicant)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity, with its kinds of entity under Article 2(1)
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc Whether its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey, that address, the main premises in Jersey, the governors' addresses in Jersey
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` interp `the entity` facts MEANS
    NOT null (`Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` interp `the entity` facts)

-- src:227 | (c) the principal address of the registered charity with the meaning of paragraph (4);
@ref Article 8(3)(c), 8(4) (src:227)
@export Whether an address is one that Article 8(4) allows as the principal address of a registered charity
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity, with its kinds of entity under Article 2(1)
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc The facts the cascade reads
      address IS A STRING @desc The address entered as the principal address
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(4) the address is a principal address of the registered charity` interp `the entity` facts address MEANS
    elem address (`Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` interp `the entity` facts)

§§ `Periods: adding years to a date (F3.4, F3.5)`

-- F3.5: a year added to a date that does not exist in the target year (29 February).  daydate's `add years` moves the day back to the last day of the month;
-- the other reading is the lenient `Date` constructor, which rolls into March.
@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F3.5 reading A: the date moves back to the last day of the month` start years MEANS
    `add years` start years

@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F3.5 reading B: the date rolls forward into the next month` start years MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY start) (DATE_MONTH start) (DATE_YEAR start PLUS years)

@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date a number of years after` interp start years MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `adding a year to a date that does not exist`
    WHEN `the date moves back to the last day of the month` THEN `F3.5 reading A: the date moves back to the last day of the month` start years
    WHEN `the date rolls forward into the next month` THEN `F3.5 reading B: the date rolls forward into the next month` start years

-- F3.4: a period of years that runs from an event on `start`.  The first day on which the period is over: the day after the anniversary if the day of the event is not
-- counted (the anniversary is then the last day of the period), the anniversary itself if the day of the event is the first day of the period.
@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F3.4 reading A: the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary` interp start years MEANS
    `the date a number of years after` interp start years PLUS 1

@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F3.4 reading B: the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary` interp start years MEANS
    `the date a number of years after` interp start years

@ref Article 8(6) (forks F3.4, F3.5)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      start IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day after a period of years from` interp start years MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `counting the day of an event in a period of years`
    WHEN `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary` THEN `F3.4 reading A: the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary` interp start years
    WHEN `the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary` THEN `F3.4 reading B: the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary` interp start years

§§ `Article 8(3)(j): whether the annual return for the most recent year has been sent`

@ref Article 8(3)(j)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Art 8(3)(j) the date on which the charity's financial year ends is not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 8(3)(j): the date on which the charity's financial year ends is not given, so the year of the annual return cannot be found"

@ref Article 8(3)(j)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Art 8(3)(j) no year of the charity has ended since it was registered` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 8(3)(j): no year of the charity has ended since it was registered, and the Law does not say what is entered about the annual return then"

-- The last day of the year that is indexed by `index` (a calendar year number) under the meaning of "year" taken.  A year is identified by its last day.
-- Calendar year: 31 December of the index.  Financial year: the charity's year-end date moved to the index (NOTHING if no year-end is given).
-- Anniversary year: the day before the anniversary of registration.
@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.2)
GIVEN index IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F3.2 reading A: the last day of the calendar year` index MEANS
    JUST (YMD index 12 31)

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.2)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      facts IS A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
      index IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F3.2 reading B: the last day of the charity's own financial year` interp facts index MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `a date on which the charity's financial year ends`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST base THEN JUST (`the date a number of years after` interp base (index MINUS DATE_YEAR base))

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.2)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
      index IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F3.2 reading C: the last day of the twelve months from an anniversary of registration` interp `the registered charity` index MEANS
    JUST ((`the date a number of years after` interp (`the registered charity`'s `date registered`) (index MINUS DATE_YEAR (`the registered charity`'s `date registered`))) MINUS 1)

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.2)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
      facts IS A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
      index IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the year of the charity indexed by` interp `the registered charity` facts index MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `meaning of the year of an annual return`
    WHEN `the calendar year` THEN `F3.2 reading A: the last day of the calendar year` index
    WHEN `the charity's own financial year` THEN `F3.2 reading B: the last day of the charity's own financial year` interp facts index
    WHEN `the twelve months from each anniversary of registration` THEN `F3.2 reading C: the last day of the twelve months from an anniversary of registration` interp `the registered charity` index

-- F3.7: which of the years that end around the day asked is "the most recent".  The list is in order of date.
@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.7)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      ends IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F3.7 reading A: the latest year that has ended before the day asked` `the day` ends MEANS
    listToMaybe (reverse (filter (GIVEN e YIELD e LESS THAN `the day`) ends))

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.7)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      ends IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F3.7 reading B: the year in progress on the day asked` `the day` ends MEANS
    listToMaybe (filter (GIVEN e YIELD e AT LEAST `the day`) ends)

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.7)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      ends IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the most recent year among` interp `the day` ends MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the most recent year`
    WHEN `the latest year that has ended before the day asked` THEN `F3.7 reading A: the latest year that has ended before the day asked` `the day` ends
    WHEN `the year in progress on the day asked` THEN `F3.7 reading B: the year in progress on the day asked` `the day` ends

-- NOTHING if the financial-year end is not given, or if the year found ended before the charity was registered (so it is not a year of the charity).
@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.7)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the most recent year of the charity` interp `the registered charity` `the day` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the most recent year among` interp `the day`
                 (mapMaybe (GIVEN k YIELD `the last day of the year of the charity indexed by` interp `the registered charity` facts ((DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 2) PLUS k)) (LIST 0, 1, 2, 3, 4))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF lastDay LESS THAN `the registered charity`'s `date registered`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST lastDay

@ref Article 8(3)(j) (fork F3.2)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      facts IS A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the financial year is meant and its year-end is not given` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `meaning of the year of an annual return`
    WHEN `the charity's own financial year` THEN NOT isJust (facts's `a date on which the charity's financial year ends`)
    WHEN `the calendar year` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the twelve months from each anniversary of registration` THEN FALSE

-- src:234 | (j) whether the registered charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year;
@ref Article 8(3)(j) (src:234)
@export Whether the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year, as at a day (Article 8(3)(j)); refuses if no year of the charity has ended since it was registered, or if the financial-year reading is asked and the year-end is not given
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (what a year is, which year is the most recent); the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including its date registered
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      facts IS A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` @desc The date on which the charity's financial year ends, and the annual returns the charity has sent with the last day of the year each relates to and the date sent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp `the registered charity` `the day` facts MEANS
    IF `the financial year is meant and its year-end is not given` interp facts
    THEN `Art 8(3)(j) the date on which the charity's financial year ends is not given`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of the most recent year of the charity` interp `the registered charity` `the day` facts
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `Art 8(3)(j) no year of the charity has ended since it was registered`
         WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
             any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `last day of the year to which it relates` EQUALS lastDay AND r's `date sent` AT MOST `the day`)
                 (facts's `annual returns sent`)

§§ `The Minister's powers to prescribe by Order (Articles 8 to 10)`

-- One shape for every power of the Minister to make an Order in Articles 8 to 10: a permission (MAY) of the Minister to make an Order about a matter.
-- It stands unexercised, and an unexercised MAY is not a breach.  The content of an Order is an input: no Order is among the sources.
@ref Article 8(3)(n), 8(5)(e), 8(6)(d), 9(1)(d), 9(2), 10(2): the Minister's powers to make an Order
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter that an Order of the Minister prescribes (Articles 8 to 10)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`the Minister may by Order prescribe` matter MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order prescribing` matter
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:238 | (n) any other information prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(3)(n) (src:238)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe other information to be entered in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3)(n))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(3)(n) the Minister may by Order prescribe other information to be entered in the register` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `other information to be entered in the register in respect of a registered charity`

-- src:248 | (e) such other matters as the Minister may prescribe by Order.
@ref Article 8(5)(e) (src:248)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe other matters to be entered in the historic section (Article 8(5)(e))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(5)(e) the Minister may by Order prescribe other matters to be entered in the historic section` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `other matters to be entered in the historic section`

-- src:253 | (d) any other document prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(6)(d) (src:253)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe other documents of which the Commissioner must retain a copy (Article 8(6)(d))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(6)(d) the Minister may by Order prescribe other documents to be retained` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `other documents of which a copy is to be retained`

§§ `Article 8(5): the five items entered in the historic section`

-- Without a recorded entry of the entity in a section, the Law does not let the encoding say whether the entity "was registered in the general section"; a missing
-- fact is not "no".
@ref Article 8(5)(b)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Art 8(5)(b) no entry of the entity in a section before deregistration is recorded` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 8(5)(b): no entry of the entity in a section of the register before its deregistration is recorded, so it cannot be said whether it was registered in the general section"

-- F3.11: "if the entity was registered in the general section".  The placements are those BEFORE deregistration (the historic entry itself is not among them).
@ref Article 8(5)(b) (fork F3.11)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.11 reading A: the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `the latest placement among` (facts's `placements of the entity before deregistration`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST latest THEN latest's `the section` EQUALS `the general section`

@ref Article 8(5)(b) (fork F3.11)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.11 reading B: any section the entity was ever entered in` facts MEANS
    any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the section` EQUALS `the general section`) (facts's `placements of the entity before deregistration`)

-- src:245 | (b) if the entity was registered in the general section, the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and any names under which it was previously so registered;
@ref Article 8(5)(b) (src:245)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(5)(b) the entity was registered in the general section` interp facts MEANS
    IF null (facts's `placements of the entity before deregistration`)
    THEN `Art 8(5)(b) no entry of the entity in a section before deregistration is recorded`
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)`
         WHEN `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration` THEN `F3.11 reading A: the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration` facts
         WHEN `any section the entity was ever entered in` THEN `F3.11 reading B: any section the entity was ever entered in` facts

@ref Article 8(5)(b) (src:245)
@export The names to be entered in the historic section for a formerly registered charity (Article 8(5)(b)): its name immediately before deregistration and its previous names, if it was registered in the general section; none if it was in the restricted section; refuses if no earlier entry of the entity in a section is recorded
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register held about the entity, with its registered name
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` @desc The entries of the entity in sections before deregistration, its previous names, matters prescribed by Order
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` interp `the registered charity` facts MEANS
    IF `Art 8(5)(b) the entity was registered in the general section` interp facts
    THEN `the registered charity`'s `registered name` FOLLOWED BY facts's `previous registered names`
    ELSE EMPTY

-- The summary of the reason (c) must include the reason for the service of the notice if the entity was deregistered for failing to comply with a required steps notice.
-- src:246 | (c) a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered, including, if that reason was a contravention of a required steps notice, the reason for the service of that notice;
@ref Article 8(5)(c) (src:246)
@export Whether the summary of the reason for deregistration must also give the reason for the service of the required steps notice (Article 8(5)(c))
GIVEN `the basis of deregistration` IS A `Basis of deregistration` @desc Why the entity was deregistered (Article 15 or 16)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(5)(c) the summary must include the reason for the service of the notice` `the basis of deregistration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the basis of deregistration`
    WHEN `the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:248 | (e) such other matters as the Minister may prescribe by Order.
@ref Article 8(5)(e) (src:248)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 8(5)(e) other matters prescribed by the Minister by Order are required` facts MEANS
    NOT null (facts's `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)`)

@ref Article 8(5)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(5)`
`the five items of Article 8(5)` MEANS
    LIST `the entity's former registered number`                                                                                                                     -- (a)
       , `the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and the names under which it was previously so registered`              -- (b)
       , `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`                                                                                                   -- (c)
       , `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`                                                                                             -- (d)
       , `such other matters as the Minister prescribes by Order`                                                                                                    -- (e)

-- Only an entity that is a formerly registered charity entered in the historic section has historic-section entries; any other standing has none.
-- src:243 | (5) The Commissioner must enter in the historic section, in relation to any formerly registered charity that has been deregistered –
@ref Article 8(5) (src:243)
@export The items the Commissioner must enter in the historic section for a formerly registered charity that has been deregistered (Article 8(5), (a) to (e)); empty if the entity is not entered in the historic section; refuses if it is, but no earlier entry of it in a section is recorded (item (b) cannot then be decided)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register held about the entity, with its standing on the register
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` @desc The entries of the entity in sections before deregistration, its previous names, matters prescribed by Order
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(5)`
`Art 8(5) the entries required in the historic section` interp `the registered charity` facts MEANS
    IF `the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register` EQUALS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
    THEN filter required `the five items of Article 8(5)`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        required item MEANS
            CONSIDER item
            WHEN `the entity's former registered number` THEN TRUE                                                                                                           -- (a)
            WHEN `the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and the names under which it was previously so registered` THEN `Art 8(5)(b) the entity was registered in the general section` interp facts   -- (b)
            WHEN `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered` THEN TRUE                                                                                         -- (c)
            WHEN `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered` THEN TRUE                                                                                   -- (d)
            WHEN `such other matters as the Minister prescribes by Order` THEN `Art 8(5)(e) other matters prescribed by the Minister by Order are required` facts          -- (e)

@ref Article 8(5)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(5)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`the Commissioner must enter in the historic section each of` items MEANS
    CONSIDER items
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN item FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `enter in the historic section an item required in respect of a formerly registered charity` item
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(5): a required item was not entered in the historic section for the formerly registered charity")
        RAND `the Commissioner must enter in the historic section each of` rest

@ref Article 8(5) (src:243)
@export The Commissioner must enter each item required by Article 8(5) in the historic section for a formerly registered charity; FULFILLED if no item is required; refuses if the entity is entered in the historic section but no earlier entry of it in a section is recorded
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register held about the entity, with its standing on the register
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` @desc The entries of the entity in sections before deregistration, its previous names, matters prescribed by Order
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(5) the Commissioner must enter in the historic section the entries required for the formerly registered charity` interp `the registered charity` facts MEANS
    `the Commissioner must enter in the historic section each of` (`Art 8(5) the entries required in the historic section` interp `the registered charity` facts)

§§ `Article 8(6): the ten-year retention of copies`

-- F3.1: from when the ten years run.  F3.4 and F3.5 settle the day on which they are over.
-- A copy of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list (for example a notice served on a governor, which Article 8(3)(k) notes but Article 8(6)(c) does not name) has no period.
-- Ten years from the deregistration of the charity: none while it is still registered.
@ref Article 8(6) (fork F3.1)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`the earliest day, ten years from the deregistration of` interp `the registered charity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the registered charity`'s `date deregistered`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
    WHEN JUST deregistered THEN `the copy may be discarded on and after` (`the first day after a period of years from` interp deregistered 10)

@ref Article 8(6) (fork F3.1)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`F3.1 reading A: ten years from the day the copy is received or made` interp copy MEANS
    `the copy may be discarded on and after` (`the first day after a period of years from` interp (copy's `date received or made`) 10)

@ref Article 8(6) (fork F3.1)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`F3.1 reading B: ten years from the day the charity is deregistered` interp `the registered charity` MEANS
    `the earliest day, ten years from the deregistration of` interp `the registered charity`

-- A copy that has not been superseded ceases to be operative with the deregistration of the charity, if it is deregistered; otherwise it is still operative.
@ref Article 8(6) (fork F3.1)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`F3.1 reading C: ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative` interp copy `the registered charity` MEANS
    CONSIDER copy's `date it ceased to be operative`
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN `the copy may be discarded on and after` (`the first day after a period of years from` interp ceased 10)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the earliest day, ten years from the deregistration of` interp `the registered charity`

-- src:249 | (6) The Commissioner must retain for 10 years, in respect of each registered charity, a copy of –
-- src:250 | (a) the constitution of the charity, and any amendments to it;
-- src:251 | (b) the annual returns of the charity;
-- src:252 | (c) any notice served on the charity under this Law; and
-- src:253 | (d) any other document prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(6) (src:249-253)
@export The first day on which the Commissioner may discard a copy of a document held in respect of a registered charity (Article 8(6)), or that it may not be discarded while the charity is registered, or that Article 8(6) does not require it to be retained
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (when the ten years begin, whether the day of the event is counted, February 29); the favoured ones apply if left out
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` @desc The copy: its kind, the date it was received or made, and the date it ceased to be operative if it did
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including the date it was deregistered if it was
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` interp copy `the registered charity` MEANS
    IF copy's kind EQUALS `a document of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list`
    THEN `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained`
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `start of the ten years of retention`
         WHEN `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy` THEN `F3.1 reading A: ten years from the day the copy is received or made` interp copy
         WHEN `from the day the charity is deregistered` THEN `F3.1 reading B: ten years from the day the charity is deregistered` interp `the registered charity`
         WHEN `from the day the copy ceases to be operative` THEN `F3.1 reading C: ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative` interp copy `the registered charity`

-- "must retain for 10 years" is the contrapositive of "must not discard before the ten years are over": a prohibition (SHANT) that sunsets when the period ends.
-- The prohibition holds through the day before the first day on which the copy may be discarded (BEFORE names the last day it holds; measured: an act on that day is a breach).
-- src:249 | (6) The Commissioner must retain for 10 years, in respect of each registered charity, a copy of –
@ref Article 8(6) (src:249)
@export The Commissioner must retain a copy of a document held in respect of a registered charity for 10 years (Article 8(6)): a prohibition on discarding it until the ten years are over
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (when the ten years begin, whether the day of the event is counted, February 29); the favoured ones apply if left out
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` @desc The copy: its kind, the date it was received or made, and the date it ceased to be operative if it did
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including the date it was deregistered if it was
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` interp copy `the registered charity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` interp copy `the registered charity`
    WHEN `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained` THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered` THEN
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        SHANT `discard a copy of a document`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(6): the copy was discarded within the retention period"
    WHEN `the copy may be discarded on and after` firstDay THEN
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        SHANT `discard a copy of a document`
        BEFORE (firstDay MINUS 1)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 8(6): the copy was discarded within the retention period"
